 in supported weeks; Useful legal-replacement production falls 13.00 points per supported week</li><li>Supported reserve coverage declines.</li><li>The supported production gain is material; the recorded roster and depth costs still matter.</li></ul><section class=\"tw-team-summary\" aria-label=\"Both teams assessment\"><section><h4>Your team \u00b7 gains and sacrifices</h4><p>Optimal legal-lineup production improves 10.00 points per supported week. Addresses supported WR lineup/depth context; package effects remain separate. Provisional: check dates and player availability.</p><p>Average optimal-lineup change across supported weeks 2, 3, 4, 5: 10</p><details><summary>Package trade-offs</summary><p>A concentrated incoming player improves supported optimal lineups; Market premium and reserve losses remain separate.</p></details></section><section><h4>Their team \u00b7 benefits and costs</h4><p>Supported counterparty effects; not a prediction of manager behavior.</p><p>Average optimal-lineup change across supported weeks 2, 3, 4, 5: 2</p><details><summary>Package trade-offs</summary><p>Supported weekly contribution is reported separately from Market price and unknown cut cost.</p></details></section></section><h4>Why</h4><ul><li>The supported production gain is material; the recorded roster and depth costs still matter.</li><li>Your optimal-lineup changes (fantasy points): Current week \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 weeks 2: 10 (conditional availability); Next-N \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 weeks 2, 3, 4: 30 (conditional availability); Rest of regular season \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 weeks 2, 3: 20 (conditional availability); Playoff window \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 weeks 4, 5: 20 (conditional availability). Separate horizons; not one combined upgrade/downgrade.</li><li>Why they may consider it: The evaluation identifies a supported benefit for their team.</li></ul><h4>Evidence confidence</h4><ul><li>Support for bounded Market/lineup conclusions; not acceptance probability or